# builtin-is-contractive returns true for a plain Dict value.
# A Dict is not a TypeNode.RecursiveRef and not a TypeNode.Union/Intersect variant,
# so it falls to the default arm (Case 2) and is treated as contractive.
# This covers the case where the argument is a Record-like structural container:
# μa.{head: Int, tail: a} — the Record wrapper shields the RecursiveRef.
[result: [builtin-is-contractive [head: "Int"  tail: "RecursiveRef"]]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})
